(Vox OS Core Utilities)
A text called "Program Version" is "0.1.10".

(Parse the flags now)
A flag called "wants help" is "--help" or "-h", it is a boolean.
A flag called "wants version" is "--version" or "-v", it is a boolean.
A text called "Program" is arguments's name.

To "show version".
  Print "{Program} (voxos) {Program Version} by Josjuar Lister".
  Exit 0.

If "wants help" then,
  Print "{Program} - create directories",
  Print "Usage: {Program} [OPTION]... DIRECTORY...",
  Print "With no DIRECTORY, or when DIRECTORY is -, read standard input.",
  Print "\nOptions:",
  Print "  -h, --help       display this help and exit",
  Print "  -v, --version    output version information and exit",
  Print "\nExamples:",
  Print "\t{Program} dir1 dir2\tCreate directories dir1 and dir2",
  Print "\t{Program} - dir3\tCreate directory dir3",
  Print "See https://github.com/vox-lang/vox for more information.",
  Exit 0.
  
Open a file for appending at 2(fd - stderr) called stderr.

To "Create a directory" with a text called "file path".
  Create a directory called 'file path'.
    On error write "{Program}: Could not create the directory at {file path}\n" to stderr.

"Create a directory" on each 'file path' from arguments's all.